{
  "_comment": "openclaw.json EXAMPLE - no secrets beyond what upstream stores here. The real file is created on the hostPath by the one-off `openclaw onboard` (operations.md 'AI ops'); this documents the steady-state shape so a restore/revert can recreate it. VERIFY every key against the pinned version's configuration reference (docs.openclaw.ai) - do not trust this shape blindly. The OPENROUTER_API_KEY is NOT here: it arrives as an env var from the openclaw-env Secret and memory search resolves keys from environment variables.",
  "gateway": {
    "mode": "local",
    "bind": "lan",
    "port": 18789,
    "controlUi": {
      "allowedOrigins": ["https://openclaw.home.jg-a.com"]
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "_comment": "OpenRouter via its OpenAI-compatible endpoint; >=64K-context model, owner's choice at onboard (D16). provider id/shape VERIFY against the pinned config reference.",
    "providers": {
      "openrouter": {
        "baseUrl": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
      }
    }
  },
  "memory": {
    "search": {
      "_comment": "D13/D15: the builtin memory engine indexes the read-only Joplin export mount via extraPaths (docs: 'the builtin engine can index directories outside the workspace with memory.search.extraPaths'). embeddings via the generic OpenAI-compatible provider -> OpenRouter (same key as chat). Pattern scopes to markdown only. VERIFY extraPaths/glob key shape + the provider block on the pinned version; fallback = keyword-only search (documented degradation).",
      "provider": "openai",
      "extraPaths": [
        { "path": "/mnt/joplin-export", "pattern": "**/*.md" }
      ]
    }
  }
}